[center][size=6][b]Custom Legendary Modifications Remade 2.0[/b][/size]
[size=3]Over 570 legendary effects for weapons and armour - craft them, or hunt for them.[/size][/center]

[size=4][b]What it is[/b][/size]
CLM adds hundreds of legendary modifications you attach at a weapons or armour workbench: elemental hits, spawned allies and enemies, grenade and mine launchers, coloured lasers, movement and stealth effects, and some that are gloriously overpowered. Simple settings decide what you get: everything free, a costly crafting game, balanced legendaries only, or a loot hunt - and a picker to show only the legendaries you want.

[size=4][b]What's new in 2.0[/b][/size]
CLM was last updated in 2017. 2.0 is a full overhaul:
[list]
[*][b]No DLC required.[/b] The main mod needs only Fallout 4 (1.09 needed all six DLC). Legendaries that use a DLC's creatures or effects are in optional, light (ESL) add-ons, one per DLC.
[*][b]Loot mode.[/b] The old "No-craft version / WIP" option, finished: legendaries drop as loose mods from anything you kill (vanilla, DLC or modded enemies), starred legendaries drop far more, family holotapes unlock crafting, and OP legendaries need a rare Legendary Core. Drop rate: Low, Standard or Higher.
[*][b]15 new legendaries[/b] built from pieces 1.09 never finished: Lobbin' mines, Hurtin' (1000%), Instant Killin', Medic's, Overchargin', VATS Penetratin', Quick Hands, Marathon Runnin', Focused, Stealth Boy'd and more.
[*][b]Coloured lasers:[/b] Green, Purple, Gold, Orange, Pink and Deep Blue, with matching beams, muzzle flashes, sparks and light.
[*][b]Dozens of fixes:[/b] legendaries that never worked now do, effects match their descriptions, free recipes that should have had a cost, and holotape menu bugs.
[*][b]Settings that work everywhere:[/b] made at any chemistry station, so PlayStation players get the full mod setup for the first time (see below).
[*][b]Legendary Picker:[/b] too many legendaries at the workbench? Pick the families you want at the chemistry station and see only those.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Fallout 4. No script extender (F4SE) needed.
[*]Add-ons (optional, each needs its DLC): [b]CLM - Automatron[/b], [b]CLM - Far Harbor[/b], [b]CLM - Nuka-World[/b], [b]CLM - Contraptions[/b]. The installer ticks the ones for the DLC you own.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Getting started[/b][/size]
Nothing to set up: a new game starts with Costly crafting and balanced legendaries (no OP ones, no variants). Attach legendaries in the "Legendary" slot of any weapons or armour workbench.

[size=4][b]Settings and the chemistry station - please read[/b][/size]
CLM's settings are [b]items[/b], not menu switches:
[list]
[*]Every setting is a weightless [b]"CLM Setting: ..."[/b] item in your Pip-Boy's Misc tab. [b]Carry it = on. Drop it (or store or sell it) = off.[/b] Carry none = the defaults.
[*]Make them for free at any [b]chemistry station[/b], category [b]"CLM Settings"[/b]: Free crafting, Loot mode, Show OP legendaries, Show variants, Hide perk-style / spawning legendaries, Picker mode, and the Low / Higher drop rate (loot mode).
[*]A setting you already carry is not offered again. Free crafting and Loot mode replace each other.
[*]PC and Xbox: the [b](CLM) Configuration Holotape[/b] (given when you leave Vault 111) gives and takes the same items from your Pip-Boy - use whichever you like.
[*]The chemistry station and workbench don't refresh while open: after a change, leave and use them again.
[*]Something missing? Check your Misc tab - Loot mode hides crafting and the picker, and an item you already carry hides its own recipe.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Legendary Picker[/b][/size]
Make [b]"CLM Setting: Picker mode"[/b] and the workbench shows only the families you pick. At the chemistry station, open a [b]CLM Armour[/b], [b]CLM Spawns[/b] or [b]CLM Weapon[/b] category and make a pick (e.g. CLM Weapon: Damage > "CLM Pick: Hurtin' (Weapon)"). Drop a pick to hide that family again; drop Picker mode to see everything. Your other settings (OP, variants) still apply; OP-only families are also under [b]CLM OP[/b].

[size=4][b]Why the chemistry station?[/b][/size]
In 1.09 the settings were holotape menus run by scripts. PlayStation mods can't use custom scripts, so on PS4 part of the mod couldn't be set up at all. Settings crafted at a chemistry station need no scripts, so 2.0 works the same on PC, Xbox and PlayStation. It's a compromise made for PlayStation players: on PC alone an F4SE menu would have been nicer, and an optional F4SE version for PC is planned for later.

[size=4][b]Upgrading from 1.09[/b][/size]
Gear with a DLC legendary attached loses it unless you install the matching add-on - take those off at a workbench before updating if you are unsure. Everything else carries over.

[size=4][b]Open source[/b][/size]
The whole mod - plugin, script sources and the tools used to build 2.0 - is on GitHub with its full history, starting from 1.09 exactly as released. Licence: CC BY 4.0 - use it in your own mods, just credit the original author.

